summary:
  Of an even count of readings the louder of the two in the middle serves.

history:
  A reading that is too loud turns the station down too far. With an advert
  at -8 on the first day and the programme at -14 on the second, the louder
  one would keep the programme 6 dB too quiet.

target:
  package/contents/ui/LoudLogic.js

find:
      return heard[Math.floor((heard.length - 1) / 2)];

replace:
      return heard[Math.floor(heard.length / 2)];

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_loudlogic.qml::test_the_number_is_the_median_of_the_readings
  and tests/qml/tst_loudlogic.qml::test_one_loud_reading_does_not_decide_once_there_are_more.
  Line-neutral.
